{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBoundedAdditiveJM","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBoundedAdditiveJM","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBoundedTheta","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAdditiveJucysMurphy"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJMB_sigma_prod_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJMB_sigma_prod_swap","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedAdditiveJM.lean#L88-L113","doc":"**The product half only swaps**: `σ_k (A_k A_{k+1}) = (A_{k+1} A_k) σ_k`.\n\nAs in the unbounded development, the recursion alone gives only the swapped form; closing it needs\nthe transposition expansion, which is the next tranche. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJMB_sigma_comm_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJMB_sigma_comm_add","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedAdditiveJM.lean#L81-L86","doc":"**`σ_k` commutes with `A_k + A_{k+1}`, for every `d`.**  The sum half of Mathas 3.24(iii). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJMB_sigma_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJMB_sigma_right","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedAdditiveJM.lean#L66-L79","doc":"**Exchange relation, right**: `A_{k+1} σ_k = h·A_{k+1} + σ_k A_k + d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJMB_sigma_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJMB_sigma_left","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedAdditiveJM.lean#L51-L64","doc":"**Exchange relation, left**: `σ_k A_{k+1} = h·A_{k+1} + A_k σ_k + d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.heckeB_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.heckeB_smul","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedAdditiveJM.lean#L46-L49","doc":"The Hecke relation in scalar-action form.  Needs `σ_i` to be a generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJMB_toBelow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJMB_toBelow","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedAdditiveJM.lean#L41-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJMB_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJMB_succ","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedAdditiveJM.lean#L38-L39","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJMB_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJMB_zero","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedAdditiveJM.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJMB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJMB","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedAdditiveJM.lean#L30-L34","doc":"**Additive Jucys–Murphy family** on a bounded presentation: `A₀ = 0`,\n`A_{k+1} = σ_k A_k σ_k + d·σ_k`.  The scalar `d` is free, exactly as in the unbounded development. ","signatureChunk":0}]}